<title>BELGIUM: NATO's Solana welcomes Bosnia vote.</title>
<headline>NATO's Solana welcomes Bosnia vote.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>NATO Secretary General Javier Solana said on Monday he was pleased with the overall conduct of elections in Bosnia at the weekend and urged newly elected officials to start working together soon.</p>
<p>In a statement, Solana said he was &quot;very proud&quot; of the role played in the elections by the NATO-led Implementation Force (IFOR).</p>
<p>&quot;IFOR's main contribution was in ensuring that the elections took place peacefully, without major incidents or disturbances,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Bosnia held its first post-war elections on Saturday.</p>
</text>
